  "id": "COMPOUND:29967 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 5-(2-Hydroxyacetyl)-10H-Phenazine-1-Carboxylic Acid and Thrombopoietin, mediated through the target entity SNU-387. This compound appears to act as a common target for multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and Bungeiside A, all of which are known to target Thrombopoietin. The shared targeting of SNU-387 by these compounds implies a possible mechanism of action that involves interaction with Thrombopoietin, possibly through a common pathway or a shared biological function. The evidence suggests that the compound in question may exert its effects by influencing SNU-387, which in turn modulates Thrombopoietin activity. This integrated pathway highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central node in the network of interactions leading to Thrombopoietin modulation.",
